vLLM 0.32.0: emit llama.cpp-style `slot print_timing` for llama-swap

llama-swap's model dashboard derives Prefill/Decode from the upstream log's
`slot print_timing` lines. vLLM never emits them, so the panel stays empty for
vLLM models (see README 'Metrics per backend'). This hook logs one pair of lines
per finished request from RequestStateStats (first_token_ts / scheduled_ts /
last_token_ts), which covers both streaming and non-streaming requests.

Format matches llama.cpp / exllama_server.py exactly so the llama-swap parser
recognises it.

Apply from site-packages: patch -p1 < this-file
Revert:                  patch -R -p1 < this-file

